From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ahmedawachi <121810925+ahmedawachi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 09:33:51 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 4/8] cygwin: log system and process commit when an allocation
 fails

What: on Cygwin/MSYS2 builds (HAVE_WIN32_MEMINFO, from the previous
patch), redisOutOfMemoryHandler() first samples win32GetSystemMemory() and
win32GetProcessMemory(). After the existing "Out Of Memory allocating N
bytes!" line, and before serverPanic(), it writes one line:

  <pid>:signal-handler (<unix time>) Out Of Memory diagnostics:
  system_commit_total=... system_commit_limit=...
  system_physical_available=... process_private_bytes=...
  process_working_set=... source=GetPerformanceInfo

All values are in bytes. The line goes through serverLogFromHandler(), the
existing async-signal-safe logger. It formats into a stack buffer and uses
open()/write(), so neither our code nor the logger allocates heap memory
after the failure. The "signal-handler" prefix is that logger's fixed
format. Other platforms are unchanged.

Why: on this platform
malloc returns NULL only after Windows has refused a commit on every
path. The log of a production crash could not say whether the host had
reached its commit limit or Redis's own commit had grown unseen. With this line, every future OOM log shows which.
errno and GetLastError() are not logged: errno is always ENOMEM, and
GetLastError() has been overwritten by the sbrk/mmap retries and the log
write.

How to trigger: the existing DEBUG OOM subcommand (zmalloc(SIZE_MAX/2))
goes through the same handler, so no new debug hook is needed. DEBUG must
be enabled (enable-debug-command).

Risk: very low. The process is about to abort anyway. If
GetPerformanceInfo fails under commit pressure, the values come from
GlobalMemoryStatusEx (source=GlobalMemoryStatusEx). If both fail they
read 0 with source=unavailable.
---
 src/server.c | 24 ++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 24 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/server.c b/src/server.c
index 933c595..8ddd83d 100644
--- a/src/server.c
+++ b/src/server.c
@@ -7877,8 +7877,32 @@ void loadDataFromDisk(void) {
 }
 
 void redisOutOfMemoryHandler(size_t allocation_size) {
+#ifdef HAVE_WIN32_MEMINFO
+    /* On Windows a failed allocation means a refused commit, so record
+     * whether the system or this process was out of commit. Sample first,
+     * before logging touches memory. errno (always ENOMEM here) and
+     * GetLastError() (already overwritten) cannot tell the cause. */
+    win32ProcessMemory pm;
+    win32SystemMemory sm;
+    win32GetProcessMemory(&pm);
+    win32GetSystemMemory(&sm);
+#endif
     serverLog(LL_WARNING,"Out Of Memory allocating %zu bytes!",
         allocation_size);
+#ifdef HAVE_WIN32_MEMINFO
+    /* The async-signal-safe logger formats into a stack buffer and writes
+     * with open()/write(), so this line needs no heap. */
+    serverLogFromHandler(LL_WARNING,
+        "Out Of Memory diagnostics: system_commit_total=%llu "
+        "system_commit_limit=%llu system_physical_available=%llu "
+        "process_private_bytes=%llu process_working_set=%llu source=%s",
+        (unsigned long long) sm.commit_total,
+        (unsigned long long) sm.commit_limit,
+        (unsigned long long) sm.phys_available,
+        (unsigned long long) pm.private_bytes,
+        (unsigned long long) pm.working_set,
+        sm.source);
+#endif
     serverPanic("Redis aborting for OUT OF MEMORY. Allocating %zu bytes!",
         allocation_size);
 }
